No Holes ("Why do crackers have holes?"), a Toon on Set film: third-party material

Font
- Baloo 2 (variable, used at weight 800) by Ek Type, SIL Open Font License 1.1. File: fonts/baloo2.ttf, from github.com/google/fonts (commit 86aced91de05cd4f96a06838124cca45be337b2b, ofl/baloo2).

Music samples (rendered with Lemo-Opuscar core/audio/sampler.py)
- VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition by Versilian Studios / Sam Gossner, CC0 1.0: violins_pizz, violins_trem, violas, violas_pizz, cellos_pizz, contrabass_pizz, bassoon_stac, clarinet_stac, tuba_stac, timpani.
- Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL), CC0 1.0: marimba, xylophone, glockenspiel, woodblock, suspended cymbal, clash cymbals.
- FreePats project (freepats.zenvoid.org), CC0 1.0: ukulele.

Voices
- Kokoro-82M (hexgrad, Apache License 2.0) through kokoro-onnx (MIT), offline: voices am_michael (narrator), af_sky (the kid), bf_isabella (grandma). Checked with faster-whisper (MIT).

Sound effects: synthesised in code (mix.py, Lemo-Opuscar core/audio/sfx.py). Everything in the picture is drawn and rendered by code.

Code
- toon.js, cast.js, card.js, set.js and caps.js come from the Toon on Set style (toon.js is adapted from Lemo-Opuscar styles/scifi-toon/demo/toon.js); the renderer uses Lemo-Opuscar core/ (core/three/post.js, core/lib.js, core/render, core/audio) and three.js (MIT).
